    "# Prototypical Networks for Few-Shot Image Classification with Explainable AI (XAI)\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📋 Research Paper-Level Documentation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Abstract\n",
    "This notebook implements a Prototypical Network-based few-shot learning system integrated with Explainable AI (XAI) techniques for medical image classification. The approach addresses the challenge of learning from limited labeled data by computing class-specific prototypes in an embedding space and performing classification based on Euclidean distance to these prototypes.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Introduction\n",
    "Few-shot learning aims to recognize novel categories from only a handful of examples. Unlike traditional supervised learning that requires thousands of samples per class, few-shot learning leverages prior knowledge from related tasks to quickly adapt to new categories. This is particularly valuable in medical imaging where annotated data is scarce and expensive to obtain.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem Setup:**\n",
    "- **N-way K-shot classification**: Given N classes with K support examples each, classify query images\n",
    "- **Support set**: Examples used to compute class prototypes\n",
    "- **Query set**: Examples to be classified\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Mathematical Formulation\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2.1 Embedding Function\n",
    "The embedding function $f_\\phi: \\mathcal{X} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^d$ maps input images to a $d$-dimensional embedding space:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{z}_i = f_\\phi(\\mathbf{x}_i) \\quad \\text{where } \\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^{H \\times W \\times C}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\phi$ represents the learnable parameters of the encoder network.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2.2 Prototype Computation\n",
    "Class prototypes are computed as the mean of support embeddings:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{p}_c = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{S}_c|} \\sum_{\\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathcal{S}_c} f_\\phi(\\mathbf{x}_i)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\mathcal{S}_c$ is the support set for class $c$ and $|\mathcal{S}_c| = K$ (number of shots).\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2.3 Distance Metric\n",
    "Classification is performed using squared Euclidean distance:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_c) = \\|\\mathbf{z} - \\mathbf{p}_c\\|^2 = \\sum_{j=1}^{d}(z_j - p_{c,j})^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2.4 Classification Logits\n",
    "Prototypical networks convert distances to logits via negative distance:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\ell_c = -d(f_\\phi(\\mathbf{x}), \\mathbf{p}_c)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The probability distribution over classes is computed using softmax:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$P(y=c | \\mathbf{x}) = \\frac{\\exp(\\ell_c)}{\\sum_{c'}\\exp(\\ell_{c'})} = \\frac{\\exp(-d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_c))}{\\sum_{c'} \\exp(-d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_{c'}))}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2.5 Loss Function\n",
    "Training uses negative log-likelihood (cross-entropy):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L} = -\\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{Q}|} \\sum_{(\\mathbf{x}, y) \\in \\mathcal{Q}} \\log P(y | \\mathbf{x})$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\mathcal{Q}$ is the query set and $|\mathcal{Q}| = N \\times Q$ (Q query examples per class).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Dataset Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset Structure:**\n",
    "- 8 classes (diseases/conditions)\n",
    "- 160 images per class\n",
    "- 128×128 pixel RGB images\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stratified Split:**\n",
    "- Training: 80% (1,024 images)\n",
    "- Validation: 10% (128 images)\n",
    "- Testing: 10% (128 images)"
   ]
