    "## 16. Research Contributions and Future Work\n",
    "\n",
    "### 16.1 Summary of Contributions\n",
    "\n",
    "This implementation demonstrates a complete prototypical network for few-shot learning with:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Efficient Architecture**: Lightweight CNN encoder (128-dim embeddings) optimized for few-shot classification\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **XAI Integration**: Grad-CAM and saliency maps provide interpretable predictions critical for medical imaging applications\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Comprehensive Evaluation**: Accuracy, F1-score, ECE for calibration, and attribution sparsity for XAI quality\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Statistical Validation**: T-tests across multiple runs ensure reproducibility\n",
    "\n",
    "### 16.2 Mathematical Contributions\n",
    "\n",
    "Key equations implemented:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Prototype computation**: $\\mathbf{p}_c = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{i=1}^{K} f_\\phi(\\mathbf{x}_i^c)$\n",
    "- **Distance metric**: $d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_c) = \\|\\mathbf{z} - \\mathbf{p}_c\\|^2$\n",
    "- **Classification**: $P(y=c|\\mathbf{x}) = \\frac{\\exp(-d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_c))}{\\sum_{c'}\\exp(-d(\\mathbf{z}, \\mathbf{p}_{c'}))}$\n",
    "- **Loss**: $\\mathcal{L} = -\\log P(y_c|\\mathbf{x}_q)$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 16.3 Limitations and Future Work\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Model Capacity**: Current 4-layer CNN may underfit complex medical images\n",
    "- **Pre-trained Backbones**: Using ImageNet pre-trained encoders (e.g., ResNet) could improve performance\n",
    "- **Episode Configuration**: 5-shot may be insufficient for highly similar classes\n",
    "- **Additional XAI Methods**: SHAP, LIME, or attention-based explanations could provide complementary insights\n",
    "\n",
    "### 16.4 References\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Snell, J., Swersky, K., & Zemel, R. (2017). Prototypical Networks for Few-shot Learning. NeurIPS.\n",
    "2. Selvaraju, R. R., et al. (2017). Grad-CAM: Visual Explanations from Deep Networks via Gradient-based Localization. ICCV.\n",
    "3. Simonyan, K., Vedaldi, A., & Zisserman, A. (2013). Deep Inside Convolutional Networks: Visualising Image Classification Models and Saliency Maps. arXiv."
   ]
